// The REGFILE interlock: a bundle that reads a register an older bundle of
// its thread will write waits until that result is back. The timing model
// counts a hazard whenever a bundle is issued while a register it reads
// still has a write outstanding: with the interlock on (the default) there
// are none; built with engine.regfile.interlock = false (Ref
// timing/README.md) the model must report exactly HAZARDS_UNLOCKED of
// them, the reads real hardware would get wrong. (The functional results
// are right either way: the model runs each thread's bundles in order.)
//
// Bundles that share no registers: no stalls and no hazards either way,
// one bundle per cycle (t2_stream's rate). WAR (a later bundle writes a
// register an earlier one reads) and registers of other threads are not
// dependences.

|| + $r1 ($i64) $r0 1 ;
|| + $r2 ($i64) $r0 2 ;
|| + $r3 ($i64) $r9 3 ;         // reads r9 ...
|| + $r9 ($i64) $r0 4 ;         // ... which this one writes: WAR, harmless
|| $halt ;
